---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const lessons = [
  {
    number: 1,
    title: "Hello, Spectrum World",
    description: "Display colourful text and control the screen with BORDER, PAPER, and INK commands.",
    status: "available"
  },
  {
    number: 2,
    title: "Screen Coordinates",
    description: "Position text anywhere on screen with PRINT AT and understand the 24×32 character grid.",
    status: "available"
  },
  {
    number: 3,
    title: "Simple Animation",
    description: "Create moving characters using PAUSE for timing and CLS for screen clearing.",
    status: "available"
  },
  {
    number: 4,
    title: "The Rubber Keyboard",
    description: "Master the unique keyword entry system where single keys enter entire commands.",
    status: "available"
  },
  {
    number: 5,
    title: "Building Patterns",
    description: "Use FOR loops and PRINT AT to create visual patterns and understand iteration.",
    status: "available"
  },
  {
    number: 6,
    title: "Graphics Characters",
    description: "Draw borders, boxes, and simple graphics using CHR$ and the Spectrum's character set.",
    status: "available"
  },
  {
    number: 7,
    title: "The Attribute System",
    description: "Understand how colours work in 8×8 pixel squares and the BRIGHT/FLASH attributes.",
    status: "available"
  },
  {
    number: 8,
    title: "Simple Sound",
    description: "Generate beeps and tones with the BEEP command for game sound effects.",
    status: "available"
  },
  {
    number: 9,
    title: "User Input",
    description: "Read keyboard input with INPUT and IF...THEN for interactive programs.",
    status: "available"
  },
  {
    number: 10,
    title: "Subroutines",
    description: "Organize code with GOSUB and RETURN for reusable program sections.",
    status: "available"
  },
  {
    number: 11,
    title: "Variables and Math",
    description: "Store data in variables and perform calculations for game logic.",
    status: "available"
  },
  {
    number: 12,
    title: "Character Movement",
    description: "Move a character around the screen with QAOP keys using INKEY$ for non-blocking input.",
    status: "available"
  },
  {
    number: 13,
    title: "Maze Runner",
    description: "Build a maze game using SCREEN$ for collision detection and wall checking.",
    status: "available"
  },
  {
    number: 14,
    title: "Collect and Score",
    description: "Add collectible items and scoring systems to track player progress.",
    status: "available"
  },
  {
    number: 15,
    title: "Enemy Chase",
    description: "Implement AI chase algorithms and lives systems for challenging gameplay.",
    status: "available"
  },
  {
    number: 16,
    title: "Spectrum Survivor",
    description: "Build a complete synthesis game combining all Tier 1 concepts into a professional title.",
    status: "available"
  }
];
---

<Layout
  title="Tier 1: Discovery - Phase 0 - ZX Spectrum"
  description="Learn ZX Spectrum programming in Sinclair BASIC. Master screen colours, text positioning, and the distinctive rubber keyboard. Build programs that run instantly—no loading required."
>
  <style>
    .course-hero {
      background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a1a1a 0%, #333333 100%);
      color: white;
      padding: var(--space-12) var(--space-4);
      text-align: center;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-12);
    }

    .course-title {
      font-family: var(--font-family-mono);
      font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem);
      font-weight: 900;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
      text-shadow: 2px 2px 4px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3);
    }

    .course-subtitle {
      font-size: 1.25rem;
      opacity: 0.95;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
    }

    .course-description {
      max-width: 700px;
      margin: 0 auto var(--space-8);
      font-size: 1.125rem;
      line-height: 1.7;
      opacity: 0.95;
    }

    .course-stats {
      display: flex;
      gap: var(--space-8);
      justify-content: center;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
    }

    .stat-item {
      text-align: center;
    }

    .stat-value {
      font-size: 2rem;
      font-weight: bold;
      font-family: var(--font-family-mono);
    }

    .stat-label {
      font-size: 0.875rem;
      opacity: 0.9;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    }

    .content-container {
      max-width: 1000px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 0 var(--space-4);
    }

    .section-title {
      font-size: 2rem;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
      color: var(--color-text);
    }

    .intro-section {
      background: var(--color-surface);
      border: 2px solid #1a1a1a;
      border-radius: 0.75rem;
      padding: var(--space-8);
      margin-bottom: var(--space-12);
    }

    .intro-section h2 {
      color: #1a1a1a;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
      font-size: 1.5rem;
    }

    .intro-section p {
      color: var(--color-text-secondary);
      line-height: 1.7;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
    }

    .intro-section ul {
      color: var(--color-text-secondary);
      line-height: 1.7;
      padding-left: var(--space-6);
    }

    .intro-section li {
      margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
    }

    .lessons-grid {
      display: grid;
      gap: var(--space-4);
      margin-bottom: var(--space-12);
    }

    .lesson-card {
      background: var(--color-surface);
      border: 2px solid var(--color-border);
      border-radius: 0.75rem;
      padding: var(--space-6);
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: auto 1fr auto;
      gap: var(--space-4);
      align-items: center;
      text-decoration: none;
      color: var(--color-text);
      transition: all var(--transition-base);
    }

    .lesson-card:hover {
      border-color: #1a1a1a;
      transform: translateX(4px);
      box-shadow: 0 4px 12px rgba(26, 26, 26, 0.1);
    }

    .lesson-number {
      width: 50px;
      height: 50px;
      background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a1a1a 0%, #333333 100%);
      color: white;
      border-radius: 50%;
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
      font-family: var(--font-family-mono);
      font-size: 1.25rem;
      font-weight: bold;
    }

    .lesson-content {
      flex: 1;
    }

    .lesson-title {
      font-size: 1.25rem;
      font-weight: 600;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-1);
      color: var(--color-text);
    }

    .lesson-description {
      color: var(--color-text-secondary);
      font-size: 0.9rem;
      line-height: 1.5;
    }

    .lesson-status {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: var(--space-2);
      font-size: 0.875rem;
      font-weight: 500;
      padding: var(--space-2) var(--space-3);
      border-radius: 9999px;
      background: rgba(26, 26, 26, 0.1);
      color: #1a1a1a;
    }

    .start-button {
      display: inline-block;
      padding: var(--space-4) var(--space-8);
      background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a1a1a 0%, #333333 100%);
      color: white;
      font-size: 1.125rem;
      font-weight: 600;
      text-decoration: none;
      border-radius: 0.5rem;
      transition: all var(--transition-base);
    }

    .start-button:hover {
      transform: translateY(-2px);
      box-shadow: 0 8px 20px rgba(26, 26, 26, 0.3);
    }

    .wow-box {
      background: var(--color-bg);
      border-left: 4px solid #1a1a1a;
      padding: var(--space-4);
      margin: var(--space-6) 0;
      border-radius: 0 0.5rem 0.5rem 0;
    }

    .wow-box strong {
      color: #1a1a1a;
      font-family: var(--font-family-mono);
    }

    .back-link {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: var(--space-2);
      color: var(--color-text-secondary);
      text-decoration: none;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
    }

    .back-link:hover {
      color: var(--color-text);
    }

    .wip-notice {
      background: #fff3cd;
      border: 2px solid #ffc107;
      border-radius: 0.75rem;
      padding: var(--space-6);
      margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
      color: #856404;
    }

    .wip-notice h3 {
      color: #856404;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
      font-size: 1.25rem;
    }

    @media (max-width: 768px) {
      .lesson-card {
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
        text-align: center;
      }

      .lesson-number {
        margin: 0 auto;
      }

      .lesson-status {
        justify-self: center;
      }
    }
  </style>

  <!-- Course Hero -->
  <section class="course-hero">
    <h1 class="course-title">TIER 1: DISCOVERY</h1>
    <p class="course-subtitle">Phase 0 - BASIC Gateway</p>

    <p class="course-description">
      The ZX Spectrum boots straight into Sinclair BASIC—no cassette loading required. You can type commands and see results instantly. Learn how to control colours with BORDER, PAPER, and INK, position text anywhere on screen, and master that distinctive rubber keyboard.
    </p>

    <div class="course-stats">
      <div class="stat-item">
        <div class="stat-value">16</div>
        <div class="stat-label">Complete Lessons</div>
      </div>
      <div class="stat-item">
        <div class="stat-value">15–25</div>
        <div class="stat-label">Minutes Each</div>
      </div>
      <div class="stat-item">
        <div class="stat-value">48K</div>
        <div class="stat-label">RAM</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Course Introduction -->
  <div class="content-container">
    <a href="/sinclair-zx-spectrum/phase-0" class="back-link">
      ← Back to Phase 0
    </a>

    <div style="background: #d4edda; border: 2px solid #28a745; border-radius: 0.75rem; padding: var(--space-6); margin-bottom: var(--space-8); color: #155724;">
      <h3 style="color: #155724; margin-bottom: var(--space-2); font-size: 1.25rem;">✅ Tier 1 Complete!</h3>
      <p>
        All 16 lessons are now available, taking you from your first PRINT statement to building complete games with character movement, collision detection, scoring, enemy AI, and professional game structure. Each lesson includes working BASIC code you can type directly into Fuse, ZXSpin, or real hardware.
      </p>
    </div>

    <section class="intro-section">
      <h2>What You'll Learn This Tier</h2>

      <p>
        Tier 1 introduces ZX Spectrum programming through Sinclair BASIC. Unlike the C64, the Spectrum boots straight into BASIC—just switch it on and start typing. These lessons teach:
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li><strong>Colour Control:</strong> BORDER, PAPER, INK for border/background/foreground, BRIGHT and FLASH attributes</li>
        <li><strong>Screen Layout:</strong> 24 rows × 32 columns of text, 256×192 pixel display, attribute system</li>
        <li><strong>Text Positioning:</strong> PRINT AT for exact row/column placement</li>
        <li><strong>Character Movement:</strong> INKEY$ for non-blocking input, QAOP movement, erase-and-redraw pattern</li>
        <li><strong>Collision Detection:</strong> SCREEN$ for reading screen contents and wall checking</li>
        <li><strong>Game Systems:</strong> Scoring, collectibles, lives, enemy AI chase algorithms</li>
        <li><strong>Sound Effects:</strong> BEEP command for game audio feedback</li>
        <li><strong>Complete Games:</strong> Professional game structure with title screens, game loops, and endings</li>
      </ul>

      <div class="wow-box">
        <strong>Tier 1 Achievement:</strong> By the end of Tier 1, you'll have mastered the Spectrum's unique attribute-based colour system, character movement with INKEY$, collision detection with SCREEN$, game scoring systems, enemy AI chase algorithms, lives systems, and complete game architecture. You'll understand why the Spectrum's instant-on BASIC environment made it perfect for bedroom coders, and you'll have built multiple complete games culminating in "Spectrum Survivor"—a professional synthesis game demonstrating all Tier 1 concepts.
      </div>

      <p>
        <strong>Prerequisites:</strong> None! Zero prior programming experience required. You'll need access to a ZX Spectrum (real hardware or emulator like Fuse). The rubber keyboard takes getting used to, but you'll master it quickly.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Lessons List -->
    <section>
      <h2 class="section-title">Lessons</h2>

      <div class="lessons-grid">
        {lessons.map(lesson => (
          <a href={`/sinclair-zx-spectrum/phase-0/tier-1/lesson-${String(lesson.number).padStart(3, '0')}`}
             class="lesson-card">
            <div class="lesson-number">{lesson.number}</div>
            <div class="lesson-content">
              <h3 class="lesson-title">{lesson.title}</h3>
              <p class="lesson-description">{lesson.description}</p>
            </div>
            <div class="lesson-status">Start →</div>
          </a>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Call to Action -->
    <section style="text-align: center; margin: var(--space-16) 0;">
      <h2 class="section-title">Ready to Start?</h2>
      <p style="color: var(--color-text-secondary); margin-bottom: var(--space-4); max-width: 600px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;">
        Switch on your Spectrum (or boot your emulator), wait for the "© 1982 Sinclair Research Ltd" message, and let's write your first line of code!
      </p>
      <a href="/sinclair-zx-spectrum/phase-0/tier-1/lesson-001" class="start-button">
        Start Lesson 1: Hello, Spectrum World
      </a>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
